{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30035 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Erysimoside appears to interact with LAMA-84 through a multi-step metabolic pathway, where it targets a dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This enzyme is subsequently engaged by multiple substrates, including Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate and N-Methyltyramine, all of which ultimately direct their targets to LAMA-84. The evidence suggests that Erysimoside may modulate LAMA-84 via indirect biochemical mechanisms, possibly by influencing the activity of the SDR family member 9, which in turn affects the downstream signaling or enzymatic pathways leading to LAMA-84 activation. The presence of multiple substrates and their shared target indicates a potential regulatory or competitive relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
